{"id":"assistant-2c3d455e-1ea2-5121-b943-71752770bfb7","sessionId":"6857faa7-23ce-b2aa-b505-6f6520514479","turnId":"turn-f660d1bd3142931a644d2d51b93ccbb8","inputEntryId":"user-turn-f660d1bd3142931a644d2d51b93ccbb8-1","createdAt":1794279988878,"updatedAt":1794279988878,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Codex CLI stores its data in `~/.codex` by default. The sandbox profile doesn't allow access to that. However, looking at the colleague's note and the kimi lane pattern, the approach is to use a scratch HOME directory. Codex CLI respects the `HOME` environment variable, so if we set `HOME` to a scratch directory, Codex will use `~/.codex` relative to that scratch home.\n\nBut wait - the sandbox profile has `(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))` which denies access to the real home passed via `-D HOME=`. The scratch HOME we create in `/tmp` is NOT the real home, so it won't be denied. The profile only denies the real home passed via `-D`.\n\nLet me re-read the kimi lane more carefully:\n\n```bash\nlocal REAL=\"$HOME\" SH; SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/khome-XXXXXX)\n( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n    env KIMI_CODE_HOME=\"$REAL/.kimi-code\" timeout $TO \"$REAL/.kimi-code/bin/kimi\" -p \"$P\" --output-format stream-json \\\n    < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n```\n\nSo:\n- `HOME=\"$SH\"` - the shell's HOME is set to the scratch directory\n- `-D HOME=\"$REAL\"` - the real home is passed as a parameter to the sandbox profile\n- The profile denies access to `(param \"HOME\")` which is the real home\n- But the shell's `HOME` is the scratch directory, which is NOT denied\n\nFor Codex, we need to do the same. But Codex also needs to write its output file. The colleague's note says Codex writes to `-o` and that fails under sandbox. So we need to:\n1. Create a scratch output directory in `/tmp`\n2. Point `-o` to that scratch directory\n3. Copy the output back after sandbox-exec\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the kimi lane - it doesn't seem to have an output file issue because Kimi's output goes to stdout (with `--output-format stream-json`). But Codex uses `-o` for its final answer.\n\nLet me now implement the `codex-sandboxed` lane:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
